KZ2 patch 2124: the live renderer's window gets a thread of its own, so no renderer wait holds its messages back.
Symptom (Proton, menu to Corinth River): at the level start the frame thread spent 8.4-9.2 s in one
pass with no message handled; Windows marks a window that has not taken a message for 5 s as "Not responding", and
close, focus and size wait. Cause: rsx_null_backend_init creates the window on its caller's thread, the port's frame
thread, whose rsx_null_backend_pump_messages is the only message loop; the same thread drains the FIFO through the
live renderer's walker, which at a cold level start waits for 100+ pipeline builds in one drain (ld_apso_await;
an earlier change's [frame-call] lines measure it). Fix (KZ2_WINDOW_THREAD, default on; 0 = the old window on the caller's
thread): rsx_null_backend_init starts a window thread that creates the window (and applies the display mode, patch
2095) and then only takes messages (MsgWaitForMultipleObjects, 50 ms at most), runs the KZ2_TEST_DISPLAY steps and
the caption. Swap-chain calls stay on the present thread: exclusive fullscreen on/off (rsx_live_draw_set_fullscreen)
is asked for by the window thread and done by the frame thread at its next rsx_null_backend_pump_messages, which
posts the result back (RSX_DM_WM_FSDONE); the window thread never waits for the frame thread (SetFullscreenState
sends messages to the window, so a wait there would deadlock). rsx_dm_apply is split into its swap-chain and window
halves for that. With the window thread, WM_CLOSE hides the window and sets window_closed (the frame thread shuts
down at its next pump, as before; DestroyWindow could pull the window from under a Present), and WM_PAINT no longer
GDI-fills over the live renderer's swap chain. [wpump] lines: the window thread's longest gap between two message
checks. Also rsx_live_draw_pso_await_totals (the walker's pipeline-build waits so far) for the port's frame-call
timing. General (upstream candidate, after patch 2095 which it changes).

